concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-1-sec-60a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "60A Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security must be"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-60a ;
    values:originalText "requested to give evidence in certain proceedings  (1) This section applies in any proceedings before the Tribunal under this Act in relation to a document that is claimed to be an exempt document under section 33.  (2) Before determining that the document is not an exempt document under section 33, the Tribunal must request the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security to appear personally and give evidence on:  (a) the damage that would, or could reasonably be expected to, be caused to:  (i) the security of the Commonwealth; or  (ii) the defence of the Commonwealth; or  (iii) the international relations of the Commonwealth;  if access to the document were given in accordance with the request; or  (b) whether giving access to the document in accordance with the request would divulge any information or matter communicated in confidence by or on behalf of a foreign government, an authority of a foreign government or an  Schedule 1  Freedom of Information Act 1982" ;
    skos:definition "requested to give evidence in certain proceedings  (1) This section applies in any proceedings before the Tribunal under this Act in relation to a document that is claimed to be an exempt document under section 33.  (2) Before determining that the document is not an exempt document under section 33, the Tribunal must request the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security to appear personally and give evidence on:  (a) the damage that would, or could reasonably be expected to, be caused to:  (i) the security of the Commonwealth; or  (ii) the defence of the Commonwealth; or  (iii) the international relations of the Commonwealth;  if access to the document were given in accordance with the request; or  (b) whether giving access to the document in accordance with the request would divulge any information or matter communicated in confidence by or on behalf of a foreign government, an authority of a foreign government or an  Schedule 1  Freedom of Information Act 1982"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "beb5cfed008fce6e0e92d928593512a9483739653022757a506e6c2009986fb9" ;
    cof:pageNumber "11"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-1-sec-60a-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-1-sec-60a-ss-2 ;
