concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-1-sec-2009-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "2009 No. 99, 2009"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-2009-4 ;
    values:originalText "(1) In determining whether the Tribunal is satisfied that it is desirable to make an order or orders under subsection 35(2) of the Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975, the Tribunal must:  (a) have regard to:  (i) the necessity of avoiding the disclosure to the applicant of exempt matter contained in a document to which the proceedings relate; and  (ii) the necessity of avoiding the disclosure to the applicant of information of the kind referred to in subsection 25(1); and  (b) where the proceedings relate to a document that is claimed to be an exempt document under section 33—give particular weight to a submission made by an agency or a Minister that it is desirable to make the order or orders under subsection 35(2) of the Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975 because disclosure of the document:  (i) would, or could reasonably be expected to, cause damage to the security, defence or international relations of the Commonwealth; or  (ii) would divulge information or matter communicated in confidence by or on behalf of a foreign government, an authority of a foreign government or an international organisation to the Government of the Commonwealth, to an authority of the Commonwealth or to a person receiving the communication on behalf of the Commonwealth or of an authority of the Commonwealth." ;
    skos:definition "(1) In determining whether the Tribunal is satisfied that it is desirable to make an order or orders under subsection 35(2) of the Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975, the Tribunal must:  (a) have regard to:  (i) the necessity of avoiding the disclosure to the applicant of exempt matter contained in a document to which the proceedings relate; and  (ii) the necessity of avoiding the disclosure to the applicant of information of the kind referred to in subsection 25(1); and  (b) where the proceedings relate to a document that is claimed to be an exempt document under section 33—give particular weight to a submission made by an agency or a Minister that it is desirable to make the order or orders under subsection 35(2) of the Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975 because disclosure of the document:  (i) would, or could reasonably be expected to, cause damage to the security, defence or international relations of the Commonwealth; or  (ii) would divulge information or matter communicated in confidence by or on behalf of a foreign government, an authority of a foreign government or an international organisation to the Government of the Commonwealth, to an authority of the Commonwealth or to a person receiving the communication on behalf of the Commonwealth or of an authority of the Commonwealth."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5ff17156e91a201c4e3f115e285af340aa587ebbd247d224b355ac1085e6a034" ;
    cof:pageNumber "14"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Tribunal must consider certain factors when deciding whether to make an order under subsection 35(2) of the Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975." ;
