concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "6 Subsection 46(1)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-6 ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the subsection, substitute:  Archives Act 1983  Schedule 2  Freedom of Information (Removal of Conclusive Certificates and Other Measures) Act 2009 No. 99, 2009            15  (1) If an application is made to the Tribunal for review of a decision refusing to grant access to a record in accordance with an application under section 40, being a record that is:  (a) claimed to be an exempt record for the reason that it contains information or matter of a kind referred to in paragraph 33(1)(a) or (b); and  (b) not a record of the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation; then the Tribunal must be constituted in accordance with subsection (2) for the purposes of any proceeding in relation to the application. Note: Section 21AB of the Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975 contains the requirements for constitution of the Tribunal in proceedings about a record of the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation that is claimed to be an exempt record for the reason that it contains information or matter of a kind referred to in paragraph 33(1)(a) or (b). Note: The heading to section 46 is replaced by the heading “Constitution of Tribunal for proceedings about certain exempt records”." ;
    skos:definition "Repeal the subsection, substitute:  Archives Act 1983  Schedule 2  Freedom of Information (Removal of Conclusive Certificates and Other Measures) Act 2009 No. 99, 2009            15  (1) If an application is made to the Tribunal for review of a decision refusing to grant access to a record in accordance with an application under section 40, being a record that is:  (a) claimed to be an exempt record for the reason that it contains information or matter of a kind referred to in paragraph 33(1)(a) or (b); and  (b) not a record of the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation; then the Tribunal must be constituted in accordance with subsection (2) for the purposes of any proceeding in relation to the application. Note: Section 21AB of the Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975 contains the requirements for constitution of the Tribunal in proceedings about a record of the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation that is claimed to be an exempt record for the reason that it contains information or matter of a kind referred to in paragraph 33(1)(a) or (b). Note: The heading to section 46 is replaced by the heading “Constitution of Tribunal for proceedings about certain exempt records”."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0b074d0e881d425f4b2655895a6fb30a606607ba93d6606aeb8300740ae968a0" ;
    cof:pageNumber "18"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Tribunal must be constituted in accordance with subsection (2) for proceedings about certain exempt records." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009.pdf> ;
    dc:source "freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009.pdf, p.18" ;
    cml:asserts concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-6-norm .
