doc:sch-2-sec-55a-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "55A(3) Automatic stay of certain decisions on appeal" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) If the Archives appeals to the Federal Court of Australia from the decision of the Tribunal and the appeal in relation to the decision is determined by the Federal Court of Australia, the stay continues to have effect until the earlier of:  (a) the time at which the decision of the Federal Court of Australia on the appeal takes effect; and  (b) the time otherwise determined by the Federal Court of Australia." ;
    cof:pageNumber "24"^^xsd:integer .

concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-55a-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "55A(4) Automatic stay of certain decisions on appeal"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-55a-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) If the Archives appeals to the Federal Court of Australia from the decision of the Tribunal and the appeal in relation to the decision is determined by the Federal Magistrates Court, the stay continues to have effect until the earlier of:  (a) the time at which the decision of the Federal Magistrates Court on the appeal takes effect; and  (b) the time otherwise determined by the Federal Magistrates Court." ;
    skos:definition "(4) If the Archives appeals to the Federal Court of Australia from the decision of the Tribunal and the appeal in relation to the decision is determined by the Federal Magistrates Court, the stay continues to have effect until the earlier of:  (a) the time at which the decision of the Federal Magistrates Court on the appeal takes effect; and  (b) the time otherwise determined by the Federal Magistrates Court."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "7d6b2200e869aed2df9e24bad2985cb915edb149b5e2e7f0e87b4998a41f1376" ;
    values:partOf concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-55a ;
    cof:pageNumber "24"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Continuation of automatic stay on appeal" ;
