concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-3-sec-21ab a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "21AB Constitution of Security Appeals Division—proceedings to"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-21ab ;
    values:originalText "review certain decisions under the Archives Act 1983 Scope  (1) This section applies to a proceeding in the Security Appeals Division in relation to a review of a decision of the Australian Archives under the Archives Act 1983 refusing to grant access to a record in accordance with an application under section 40 of that Act, being a record that is:  (a) a record of the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation; and  (b) claimed to be an exempt record for the reason that it contains information or matter of a kind referred to in paragraph 33(1)(a) or (b) of that Act. Constitution of Security Appeals Division  (2) Subject to this section, the Security Appeals Division is to be constituted by:  (a) 3 presidential members; or  (b) a presidential member alone. When presidential member must not participate  (3) A presidential member must not participate in the proceeding if he or she is, or has been, the Director-General of Security or an  Schedule 3  Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975" ;
    skos:definition "review certain decisions under the Archives Act 1983 Scope  (1) This section applies to a proceeding in the Security Appeals Division in relation to a review of a decision of the Australian Archives under the Archives Act 1983 refusing to grant access to a record in accordance with an application under section 40 of that Act, being a record that is:  (a) a record of the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation; and  (b) claimed to be an exempt record for the reason that it contains information or matter of a kind referred to in paragraph 33(1)(a) or (b) of that Act. Constitution of Security Appeals Division  (2) Subject to this section, the Security Appeals Division is to be constituted by:  (a) 3 presidential members; or  (b) a presidential member alone. When presidential member must not participate  (3) A presidential member must not participate in the proceeding if he or she is, or has been, the Director-General of Security or an  Schedule 3  Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d486d5b6439f87c6defe8cbf2ef6f0ad9571fbb43190688ad4cbd07297fb4fa9" ;
    cof:pageNumber "27"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-3-sec-21ab-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-3-sec-21ab-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-3-sec-21ab-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
